Repeated incorrect outputs indicate the task class or answer representation may be wrong, not merely a coordinate detail. Before spending another attempt, revisit all demonstrations: list input/output dimensions, identify separators and partitions, enumerate each region's candidate features, and test a compact region-summary mapping across every pair. Do not submit a revised pattern unless it exactly reproduces all known demonstrations. A new demo request should target a clearly stated unresolved distinction; serial requests without analysis impose cost without improving inference.

