When demos show sparse markers receiving copies of an embedded motif, distinguish the motif's bounding-box origin from the motif coordinate aligned with a marker. Represent that alignment as a signed offset and validate it against multiple marker/copy pairs. Replay every marker footprint against the complete demo output, including source motif retention, overlaps, clipping, and unchanged candidate markers.

A common failure is to shift a plausible template by intuition (top-left, center, or a salient source pixel) without validating the anchor. After incorrect feedback, discard that placement hypothesis and re-derive the offset from observed coordinate correspondences. Validate serialization independently: row widths and legal values must be checked before submission.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-ws0/frozen/seen-2/play/users/u045/system/state/hermes/skills/puzzle-solving/arc-stream-demo-discipline/references/marker-anchor-offsets.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "arc-demo-delta-discipline", "file": "references/session-task-4f5f6fe0-review.md", "content": "# Recurrent task reference-transfer failure

This instance reused task ID `task-4f5f6fe0` but had a different geometry from the remembered ray-extension example. A prior reference described a diagonal continuation rule for a 14×25 scene; the current test was 23×6, and the available demo was 26×24 with a diagonal ray from a motif endpoint. Treating the reference as ground truth led to multiple unsupported test submissions: first a single-cell recoloring, then diagonal extensions, and then retries that adjusted local placements/colors without evidence. The second demo did show a diagonal ray (color 6) continuing from a compact motif toward the top-left boundary, but it did not validate the assumed test transformation.

Reusable lesson: same task ID and superficially related rays are not proof of a shared rule. Before transferring a session reference, replay its abstract rule against every current demo, including direction, source endpoint, marker/template roles, retained cells, color behavior, dimensions, and boundary termination. If the rule fails exact replay or does not constrain the test, treat the test as unresolved. After incorrect feedback, avoid cosmetic variants; request a demo only for a concrete ambiguity or reassess representation/task class. This transcript did not establish a validated test solution.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-ws0/frozen/seen-2/play/users/u045/system/state/hermes/skills/puzzle-solving/arc-demo-delta-discipline/references/session-task-4f5f6fe0-review.md"}

{"success": true, "name": "arc-task-delta-inference", "file": "references/compact-output-reassessment-after-errors.md", "content": "# Compact-output reassessment after incorrect submissions

When inputs are partitioned by repeated separator rows or columns but demos produce much smaller outputs, dimension ratios help identify possible structure but do not establish the encoding. Keep distinct hypotheses for (a) summarizing interior regions, (b) recording separator/boundary markers at their intersections, and (c) selecting only rows or columns with special markers. For each demo, write down the exact partition counts and map candidate input coordinates or blocks to each output cell, including ordering. Reproduce every output exactly before transferring the map.

After an incorrect compact-output submission, do not merely alter colors or copy another visually salient set of markers. Reopen the task class and output representation, and re-derive dimensions and correspondence from all demos. Repeated, heterogeneous demos may share only an abstract structure; spend another demo only when two explicit mappings predict a materially different discriminating observation.", "file_type": ".md", "_source_path": "/home/USER/continual-arc-baselines/.workbench/stage1/H-hermes-luna6-low-ws0/frozen/seen-2/play/users/u045/system/state/hermes/skills/puzzle-solving/arc-task-delta-inference/references/compact-output-reassessment-after-errors.md"}

